A||||24||Rare87GT||Lowering Springs or Cutting Springs||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||10-31-2001||02:28 AM||||Well I was reading the last post about lowering a Fiero correctly and was needing some advice.  I know cutting the springs will most likely ruin the caster/camber, but the right way would be with Eibach Springs if I am right.  What are the chances that my car if I lower it 1.5" turns into a civic hopping machine or will I be fine cutting it that length.  I know if I screw up or something I can get the springs off of a Fiero at a junkyard, just wanted to know the preference of most people on the board.  If not, how much do a set of Eibach lowering springs cost for a Fiero?  Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroX||10-31-2001||02:44 AM||||go to bed||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||10-31-2001||03:06 AM||||...<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||10-31-2001||03:07 AM||||I wouldn't cut the springs.. If you enjoy driving it, I would get a good set of springs. The best way (I hear..) is to use drop spindles on front & coilovers on the rear. (I'm using Eibach's all around on one of my cars. No complaints here)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good Luck ... <BR><FONT COLOR="purple"><B><I>-Haze</I></B></FONT>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">  <P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">                 .                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||6
Z||000004||MrPBody||10-31-2001||09:18 AM||||Either way works.  Lowering springs probably are better; cutting is cheaper.  Either way, you'll have to align it after lowering.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Smoooooth GT||10-31-2001||09:27 AM||||HHmmm.. Are there any spring off of anyother car that would *act* like lowering spring's, we would'nt have to cut them, and still act like shorter spring's???  Thank's Steve<P>------------------<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||TRiAD||10-31-2001||09:31 AM||||Well, I said this last time, but...<BR>It's your skin. What's it worth to you?<BR>Go Eibach. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WhiteFieroBlur||10-31-2001||11:58 AM||||Well my next thing I am doing is lowering and I been doing some searching and research on it. As everyone knows your best bet is coilover and spindles. But if your like me there is no way I can afford that. If I could I might as well get a paint job. I wanna go with cutting only because the fierostore springs say they lower it one inch and I don't think thats enough. I wanna go atleast 1.5 or 2. But to be on the safe side I am proably gonna go with the springs. I know some people have proablems with cutting and some people never. I just can't afford it going bad from cutting.<P> If anyone knows of springs that lower more than 1 inch let me know.<P>and here is the thread I just made on the subject <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011416.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011416.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||filthyscarecrow||10-31-2001||12:45 PM||||my dad cut the springs on his 86SE. <BR>just hacked one coil off the front and it looks kickass, the front springs are a little stiffer because the spring rate changed a bit, but not enough to need stiffer dampers. you will have to align the car, both toe and camber. castor is not affected by cutting the spring, only by moving the washers that space the upper a-arm. <BR>i'm not sure how much one is suppposed to cut off the rears though. you might have to try that one little by little... start with somehting like 1/2 to 3/4 coil, put them back on adn see where it sits. i would think 1 coil would be sufficient. oh yeah, and get a good saw blade. it's not as easy as it sounds... ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rare87GT||10-31-2001||03:22 PM||||I did go to bed.||||reg||1
